Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): refuse unknown bare gateway ownership before
 pre-swap [daveey]

Root (happened): _discover_bare reused best-effort service PID and home partition filters, so an unknown gateway vanished before the strict pause could refuse it. The user-unit default-home inference could likewise turn unknown ownership into an exclusion.

Root (not caught): previous strict-discovery tests replaced _discover_bare. Exercise real discovery through _pause with synthetic OS probes and only the stop mutation seam replaced.

Recurrence: follows 5f002239a22 strict systemd inventory correction; the manual-discovery and implicit-default exclusion branches remained best effort.

Proof: r6-red-run2 reproduced six bare-discovery failures; r6-default-red-run4 reproduced implicit-default silent success. Strict opt-in now uses only transaction-owned service PIDs, explicit home classification and proven foreign-code exclusions. Default behavior remains unchanged. Canonical final run r6-final-run7: five focused files pass; no process signals or service mutations were performed.
